  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Tennessee totaled $10.5B in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 3.9% year over year. Contracting activity reached 17,965 awards with an average award size of $586K. The Department of Energy dominates buying in the state, obligating $6.9B, which makes up the largest share of the total. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $5.8B, reflecting large operations, maintenance, and site-support work. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC and UT-BATTELLE LLC are the top vendors, with $3.1B and $2.6B respectively. Remediation Services and Engineering Services are the second and third largest industries, at $723M and $688M respectively. The Department of Defense, Department of Justice, and Department of Veterans Affairs follow the Department of Energy among buying agencies, with $1.4B, $716M, and $515M respectively. Construction, security, and specialized chemical and credit-related activities also appear on the industry leaderboard. These figures are fiscal year to date totals and represent contract obligations, so current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal buying in Tennessee?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer, obligating $6.9B. The Department of Defense obligated $1.4B and the Department of Justice obligated $716M. Facilities Support Services leads industries with $5.8B, showing concentration in a few large program areas."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the biggest contracts in Tennessee?",
        "body": "CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC captured $3.1B and UT-BATTELLE LLC captured $2.6B. UNITED CLEANUP OAK RIDGE LLC captured $559M and METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. captured $515M. Top vendors align with the largest industries and the Department of Energy buying profile."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Tennessee?",
      "a": "Tennessee received $10.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 17,965 awards with an average award size of $586K, and obligations were down 3.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Tennessee?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy is the largest contracting agency, obligating $6.9B. The Department of Defense obligated $1.4B, the Department of Justice obligated $716M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $515M; other buyers include Department of Health and Human Services at $251M and Department of Homeland Security at $202M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Tennessee?",
      "a": "CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC is the largest federal contractor in Tennessee, with $3.1B in obligations. UT-BATTELLE LLC follows with $2.6B, and UNITED CLEANUP OAK RIDGE LLC and METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. reported $559M and $515M respectively."
